Findings (reproduce: build-rel/release/fuzz-<bin> run <target> <file>; build with ./build.sh rel fuzz-<bin>)
1 containment: a "/" followed by a combining mark is one Character, so Character-based splitting does not see the separator and a leading ".." survives.
  Archives/ArchiveTree.swift:82 (normalized), FileTools/Transcoding.swift:520 (safeName), FileTools/SplitCombine.swift:242 (stored name).
  repro/arch/containment-slash-combining-mark.zip|.tar (fuzz-arch zip|tar), repro/tools/decode-containment-slash-combining-mark.bin (fuzz-tools decode),
  repro/tools/combine-containment-slash-combining-mark.crc (fuzz-tools combine). Result: one file written into the parent of the target folder.
  Fix: split and compare on utf8 bytes (as RemoteEntry.isSafeName does), and check the final URL stays below the target.
  Same class, no write: Network/ServerAddress.swift:65 RemotePath.normalized (repro/net/remotepath-slash-joins-combining-mark.bin, fuzz-net address).
2 crash: Network/ServerAddress.swift:48 components.port = port with a negative saved port (URLComponents traps). repro/net/saved-connection-port-trap.json (fuzz-net saved).
3 hang: Network/FTPListParser.swift:126-130 regexes used by unix() (~:153); a LIST line with a long digit run backtracks: 250/500/1000/2000 digits = 15/56/217/991 ms.
  repro/net/ftplist-regex-backtracking.txt (fuzz-net ftplist, add --timeout 0.5).
4 low: FileTools/ChecksumFiles.swift:133-136 yields an entry with an empty name for "<digest> *". repro/tools/checksum-empty-name.md5 (fuzz-tools checksum).
5 low, PanelModel (fuzz-kernel panel): repro/kernel/panel-selection-set-loses-twin-names.bin (selection: Set<String> merges NFC/NFD twins, PanelModel.swift:97-102);
  panel-selectioncount-vs-marked.bin (a mark without a shown row after setSort); panel-computed-size-shown-vs-listed.bin (setComputedSizes, :712-720). Root cause of the last two not analysed.
Not a product bug: runs/net-address-driver-artifact (driver passed an empty default scheme).
